r lips; Suniti-Suniti;\nUtsange in his lap; Udhoya--lifted up; Balam--son; Nishamy--heard; Tat-Paur-Mukhat--from the mouth of other relatives;\nNitantam-All the news; Sa--He; Vivyathe--became sad; Yat-Which; Gaditam-Said; Sa-Palya-By the daughter-in-law..\n\nWhen Dhruva Maharaj came to his mother, her lips were trembling with anger, and she\nwas sobbing loudly. Queen Suniti immediately picked up her beloved in her lap.\nAnd the residents of the inner chambers narrated in detail all the bitter words that Suruchi had heard. In this way, Suneeti became extremely sad.\nWith a sigh, she lamented with patience and grief.\nLike a child thrown into a fire.\nThe sentence remembers the lotus flowers.\nThe state of Shriya is like a cloud. 16). Meaning of the word\nSa--He; Utsrijya--leaving; Dheerdham--patience, grew; Vilapa--started lamenting; Shoka-daav-agnina- from the fire of grief;\nDaav-lata-iva--like burnt leaves; Balaa--Satri; Vakyam-word; Sa-palyah--said by one's co-wife; Smarati--\nRemembering; Saroj-shriya-like beautiful face; Dasha-looking; Bashya-kalam-crying; Uvah-said..\nThis incident was unbearable for Suniti. She was as if burning in a fire of sorrow, and because of the\ncause, she became like a burnt leaf (Beli), and began to regret. By remembering her sister-in-law's\nwords, her lotus-like beautiful face filled with tears, and she spoke in this way.\nMeaning: When a person is sad, he feels like a burnt leaf from the fire of the forest.\nAnother word: When a person is sad, he feels like a burnt leaf. Such was the situation of Sunithi. Although Suniti's face was like a lotus,\nbeautiful, but from the fire caused by the bitter words of her lover, it withered.\nLong breath, the end of the suffering.\nThe child sees the child.\nTHE father is in the other, the mind.\nUg, the one who is in the other's suffering. 97 Lexicon"},{"pageNumber":2836,"text":"220\nदीर्घमू--अत्यधिक; श्वसन्ती--साँस लेती हुई; वृजिनस्य--संकट की; पारम्‌- सीमा; अपश्यती--बिना पाये; बालकम्‌--अपने\n